# Cloudflare Pages / Redirects
# NOTE: Cloudflare Pages serves .html files at clean URLs natively (pretty URLs).
# Do NOT add /page → /page.html redirects — they cause redirect loops.
# Only list non-trivial slugs here.

/meet-angelique          /index.html             301
/support-group-inquiry   /support-groups.html    301
/reproductive-support    /services.html          301
/intended-parent         /services.html          301
/surrogate-assessment    /services.html          301

# www → non-www. This rule was here but without the trailing "!", so it never
# fired: www.pivotaltides.com was serving the entire site with a 200 alongside
# the non-www copy. Canonicals all say non-www. The "!" forces the redirect to
# win over a matching static file, which is what makes it work on Pages.
https://www.pivotaltides.com/*  https://pivotaltides.com/:splat  301!
